From 95179f67b22a26601c35484e64edfeaf2bc4cfa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:19:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: runtime shared by the behaviours, the
 models and the material properties

- the backends of the generic-parallel interface for material
  properties write the code of the behaviours and of the models too
  (runtime of the interface, shared data copied to the device, names of
  the generated files).
- statistics of the synchronous computations held by blocks of a pool
  (StatisticsBlock): the atomic operations are performed in device
  memory, and the device signals an event to the host by a flag in
  pinned memory, so that a call without event performs neither copy nor
  additional synchronization.
- function object of the CUDA kernels declared __grid_constant__: its
  member functions take its address, which made each thread copy it in its
  stack (more than a kilobyte per thread for a behaviour).
- the material properties may also contain the function of the generic
  interface (generic_functions option).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
